📅 12‑Week MySQL Roadmap
Month 1: Fundamentals & Revision
Week 1
Learn/revise SELECT, WHERE, ORDER BY, LIMIT.
Practice filtering and sorting data from sample tables.

Week 2
Master JOINs: INNER, LEFT, RIGHT.
Practice combining data from multiple tables (employees + departments).

Week 3
Aggregations: COUNT, SUM, AVG, MIN, MAX.
Grouping with GROUP BY and filtering with HAVING.

Week 4
Subqueries: nested queries for filtering and aggregations.
Practice writing queries that answer business questions.

Month 2: Intermediate Concepts
Week 5
Views: create reusable query results.
Practice building views for reporting.

Week 6
Indexes: clustered vs. non‑clustered, query optimization.
Compare query performance with and without indexes.

Week 7
Stored Procedures & Functions: automate repetitive tasks.
Write a procedure to calculate monthly sales totals.

Week 8
Transactions: BEGIN, COMMIT, ROLLBACK.
Practice ensuring data consistency in multi‑step operations.

Month 3: Advanced Topics & Admin
Week 9
Triggers: automate actions when data changes.
Example: log updates to a table in an audit table.

Week 10
Schema Design & Normalization (1NF → 3NF).
Design a normalized database for an e‑commerce app.

Week 11
Partitioning & Sharding basics for large datasets.
Learn how MySQL handles big data scaling.

Week 12
Performance tuning: EXPLAIN plans, query rewriting.
User management, roles, privileges, backups (mysqldump).

📚 Where to Learn MySQL (Step by Step)
1. Fundamentals (Weeks 1–4)
Official MySQL Documentation → dev.mysql.com/doc  
Best for syntax reference and examples.

FreeCodeCamp YouTube Course → “MySQL Full Course” (4–hour beginner friendly).

W3Schools MySQL Tutorial → w3schools.com/mysql  
Quick, interactive lessons with practice queries.

2. Intermediate Concepts (Weeks 5–8)
Khan Academy SQL Course → Covers joins, subqueries, and aggregations interactively.

LeetCode SQL Practice → Real interview‑style SQL problems.

Udemy Course → “The Complete SQL Bootcamp” by Jose Portilla (paid, but very popular).

3. Advanced Topics & Admin (Weeks 9–12)
MySQL Performance Blog (Percona) → Deep dives into indexing, optimization, and scaling.

Coursera Specialization → “Databases for Data Scientists” (University of Colorado).

YouTube Channels → “TechTFQ” and “Programming with Mosh” for triggers, transactions, and schema design.

🛠️ Practice Platforms
SQLZoo → Interactive exercises.

Hackerrank SQL Track → Practice problems with instant feedback.

Mode Analytics SQL Tutorial → Business‑oriented SQL queries.

🚀 How to Use These Resources
Spend 15–20 min watching/reading theory (YouTube, docs, tutorials).

Spend 20–30 min practicing queries on Hackerrank/LeetCode/SQLZoo.

Apply weekly concepts to a mini project (like an e‑commerce database).



Best YouTube channels for learning MySQL are FreeCodeCamp, Programming with Mosh, and Alex the Analyst. For practicing MySQL in real time, OneCompiler and HackerRank are excellent platforms.

